    {
      "title": "Union-Find (Disjoint Set Union)",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Union-Find (Disjoint Set Union)",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Model and Mechanism",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Disjoint sets== in a `parent` array; `parent[x]==x` marks a ==root==",
                "`find(x)` gives the root; `union(a,b)` merges sets"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Path compression==: `parent[x]=find(parent[x])`",
                "==Union by size==: smaller tree under larger",
                "Together: amortized ==O(α(n))==, near constant"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def find(x):",
                "    if parent[x] != x: parent[x] = find(parent[x])",
                "    return parent[x]",
                "def union(a, b):",
                "    a, b = find(a), find(b)",
                "    if a == b: return False",
                "    if size[a] < size[b]: a, b = b, a",
                "    parent[b] = a; size[a] += size[b]; return True"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Use and Kruskal",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Union-find",
                "Rerun BFS/DFS"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Edge added: connected?",
                  "O(α(n))",
                  "O(V+E) each time"
                ],
                [
                  "Split sets, delete edges",
                  "{red:No}",
                  "Rebuild"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Sort edges by weight",
                "Keep an edge only if `find(u)!=find(v)`, then `union`",
                "Equal roots: edge closes a ==cycle=="
              ],
              "style": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`union` on raw nodes, not `find()` roots",
                "No compression and no union by size: find is O(n); size alone gives O(log n)",
                "`parent[i]` not set to `i`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
